(5249892, 762195, 27845, '<td valign="top">Yeah, gudd geschafft an gudd verdéngt! Ech mengen d''Versioun ouni Faarw wier net souwäit komm, mee déi hei huet den néidegen *boom* Effekt.</td>', 'Yeah, gudd geschafft an gudd verdéngt! Ech mengen d''Versioun ouni Faarw wier net souwäit komm, mee déi hei huet den néidegen *boom* Effekt.', '2009-02-11 06:27:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5249918, 760868, 99506, '<td valign="top"><br/>Hey Laura<br/> <br/>Well done with your first entry, you scored higher than I did with my first.<br/> <br/>I''ve looked at your settings and with a shutter speed of 1/32s I think the focus problem is likely to be due to camera shake.<br/> <br/>Try aperture priority and set to something like F16 or higher to get a better depth of field and hence more focus from foreground to background.<br/> <br/>Personaly I prefer to use a lower ISO as well to reduce noise.<br/> <br/>The only issue with what I''m sugesting is that you would most likely need to pop your camera on a tripod or at least balance it on something and use the timer.<br/> <br/>Hey and now you have some software try using an Unsharp Mask<br/></td>', 'Hey Laura Well done with your first entry, you scored higher than I did with my first. I''ve looked at your settings and with a shutter speed of 1/32s I think the focus problem is likely to be due to camera shake. Try aperture priority and set to something like F16 or higher to get a better depth of field and hence more focus from foreground to background. Personaly I prefer to use a lower ISO as well to reduce noise. The only issue with what I''m sugesting is that you would most likely need to pop your camera on a tripod or at least balance it on something and use the timer. Hey and now you have some software try using an Unsharp Mask', '2009-02-11 07:28:04.000000', NULL, 0),
